  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN days, and the sell price of a watch on the iii-th day is AiA_iAi​. Initially you have 000 watches.\n\nFor each day from 111 to NNN, the following events happen:\n\n\nFirst, you acquire one watch for free on each day.\nNext, you may choose to sell **upto 222 watches** (that you own) for AiA_iAi​ coins each.\nWhat is the maximum profit you can obtain by optimally selling items?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum profit you can obtain.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤1071 \\le A_i \\le 10^71≤Ai​≤107"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n1 2 3\n3\n3 2 1\n4\n2 7 3 5",
        "output": "8\n6\n24",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : The optimal approach is as follows:\n\nSell nothing on day 111.\nSell one watch on day 222 for 222 coins.\nSell 222 watches on day 333 for 666 coins.\n\nTest Case 2 : We should sell 111 watch on each day for 3+2+1=63 + 2 + 1 = 63+2+1=6 coins."
      }
    ]
  },
